# The n-th Fibonacci number, F(0) = 0, F(1) = 1, iteratively, as i64.
# Rosetta Code: Fibonacci_sequence. Exercises: mutable locals, times.

: fib ( i32 -- i64 )
  :> n
  0 i64 :> a!
  1 i64 :> b!
  n [ drop  a b i64.add :> c  b a!  c b! ] times
  a ;
test fib : 0 fib -> 0 i64
test fib : 1 fib -> 1 i64
test fib : 2 fib -> 1 i64
test fib : 10 fib -> 55 i64
test fib : 90 fib -> 2880067194370816120 i64   # the largest asked for

: main ( -- )
  21 [ :> i  "F(" print i i32.to-str print ") = " print i fib i64.to-str println ] times ;
